// Third player-authored RapidRanged spell in this folder, same shape as
// eldritch_blast.ron/wayward_force_darts.ron (both circle 0/1). See
// eldritch_blast.ron's own header for the full reasoning on why
// RapidRanged fires every projectile along the SAME
// data.inputs.look_dir -- there is no per-projectile independent aim in
// common/src/states/rapid_ranged.rs, so the sheet's "each streaking at a
// target of your choice" (implying 3 independently-aimed rays that could
// hit 3 different creatures) is not modeled; in practice all 3 rays land
// on whichever single target the caster is looking at. `damage_kind:
// Fire` is exactly representable here (RapidRanged's
// `projectile.attack.damage_kind` is fully RON-configurable, unlike
// BasicMelee/Explosion/GroundAoe/BasicBeam, which all hardcode their
// DamageKind in Rust).
//
// Circle 2, scaled up from wayward_force_darts (circle 1: 3 darts, 6
// dmg/dart, 10 energy/dart = 30 total) -- 3 rays, 9 dmg/ray (27 total),
// 14 energy/ray (42 total). Flagged for wave-close-out balance review
// alongside this cell's other first-of-kind numbers.
RapidRanged(
    energy_cost: 14,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    shoot_duration: 0.05,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    options: (
        max_projectiles: Some(3),
        fire_all: true,
    ),
    projectile: (
        kind: Simple,
        attack: Some((
            damage: 9,
            damage_kind: Fire,
        )),
    ),
    projectile_body: Object(BoltFire),
    projectile_speed: 80.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
